<title>USA: Dayton Hudson to appeal tax court ruling.</title>
<headline>Dayton Hudson to appeal tax court ruling.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dayton Hudson Corp said Friday it plans to appeal a U.S. Tax Court decision that could result in the company owing up to $60 million in taxes and interest.</p>
<p>The company did not expect the payment to affect its results from operations even if it loses the appeal, according to a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The retailer said a U.S. Tax Court last week ruled in favor of the U.S. Internal Revenue Service, which challenged Dayton Hudson's practice of taking deductions for inventory shortage expenses for income tax purposes.</p>
<p>Dayton Hudson said its potential liability is related to timing differences, and the rest, if any, will be charged against reserves.</p>
<p>(( -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787 ))</p>
